---
/**
 * GoHighLevel chat, deferred until the visitor does something.
 *
 * Loading it normally costs the page its Total Blocking Time (currently 0 ms)
 * and a chunk of LCP — GHL's loader pulls 150–300 KB of third-party JS. Nobody
 * opens a chat widget in the first 300 ms, so nothing is lost by waiting for the
 * first scroll, pointer move or touch. A hard timeout backstops the case where a
 * visitor reads without interacting at all.
 *
 * Renders nothing at all when no widget id is configured.
 */
const { widgetId, location, timeout = 6000 } = Astro.props;
---
{widgetId && (
  <script is:inline define:vars={{ widgetId, location, timeout }}>
    (function () {
      var loaded = false;
      function load() {
        if (loaded) return;
        loaded = true;
        events.forEach(function (e) { window.removeEventListener(e, load); });
        var s = document.createElement('script');
        s.src = 'https://widgets.leadconnectorhq.com/loader.js';
        s.setAttribute('data-resources-url', 'https://widgets.leadconnectorhq.com/chat-widget/loader.js');
        s.setAttribute('data-widget-id', widgetId);
        if (location) s.setAttribute('data-location-id', location);
        s.async = true;
        document.body.appendChild(s);
      }
      var events = ['scroll', 'pointermove', 'touchstart', 'keydown'];
      events.forEach(function (e) {
        window.addEventListener(e, load, { once: true, passive: true });
      });
      setTimeout(load, timeout);
    })();
  </script>
)}

{/* There is deliberately no stylesheet here.

    A rule used to sit at this spot trying to lift GHL's bubble clear of the
    sticky call bar on phones — `.lc_text-widget--wrapper`, `#lc_text-widget--root`
    and `div[id^="lc_text-widget"]` at `bottom: 4.6rem !important`. It never did
    anything, for two independent reasons, and nobody noticed because Oakville
    was the only entity with a widget until 2026-08-06.

    1. GHL renders into a <chat-widget> custom element with a SHADOW ROOT. Page
       CSS cannot cross that boundary. `is:global` does not help — sealing the
       widget off from page styles is the entire purpose of a shadow root.
    2. The selectors were wrong regardless. The real element is `.lc_text-widget`
       with `.lc_text-widget--bubble` inside it, both classes, no such ids.

    Injecting a stylesheet into the shadow root does work — measured, bubble
    moved to 88px — but it means depending on a third party's internal class
    names from outside, which breaks silently the day GHL renames one. The usual
    alternative, a `transform` on the host to make it a containing block, is
    worse: the host is `display: inline`, zero-size, and appended wherever the
    loader landed (measured 21373px down the page), so fixed children would
    position against that instead of the viewport.

    GHL exposes ~25 `--chat-widget-*` custom properties for colour, width and
    height, and none for position. Nick confirmed 2026-08-06 that the platform
    has no offset setting either.

    So the bubble stays where GHL puts it — bottom right, 20px in, 58px across —
    and the SITE moves instead. StickyCall.astro reserves that footprint when a
    chat widget is configured. Fix it there, not here. */}
